{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "חמץ דם זבחי", :translit "chametz dam zivchai", :gloss "leaven [with] blood of My sacrifice"} {:he "מחצי היום", :translit "machtzi ha-yom", :gloss "half of the day"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "חמץ דם זבחי", :b "מחצי היום"}], :frame {:text "The verse prohibits slaughtering the Paschal offering while leaven is still present. The Mishnah states that the daily afternoon tamid offering, whose slaughter permits the Paschal offering to be slaughtered, may be slaughtered from six and a half hours onward (midday minus a half hour), i.e., after 'half the day' has passed (Pesachim 61a, Pesachim 5:1). The Ba'al HaTurim encodes this halakhic timestamp — machtzi ha-yom, 'half the day' — into the gematria of the verse's own words.", :sources ["Mishnah Pesachim 5:1" "Pesachim 61a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "חמץ דם זבחי", :a-value 209, :b "מחצי היום", :b-value 209, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:20:56.690285141Z", :model "glm-5.2"}